# Small talk: the everyday between any two residents, anywhere. Varied by who they are to each other (band), their
# ages and trades, the hour and the place. Scenes for one region live in regions/; these are for anywhere.

scene st_morning_greeting
when topic=smalltalk time=dawn
a[old] : Up before the birds again, {b}. My bones won't let me sleep. | Morning, {b}. The cold gets in early at my age.
a[child] : Morning, {b}! | Good morning, {b}! Have you eaten yet?
a : Morning, {b}. | Early start for you too, {b}? | Morning. Sleep well?
b[child] : I'm not tired at all! | Mama says I have to be useful today.
b[strangers] : Morning. | Good morning to you.
b[old] : Morning. Ask me again when the sun's properly up.
b : Morning. Barely. | Well enough. You? | Morning, {a}. Another day of it.
a?[friends] : Come and find me at midday; I'll have bread to spare.

scene st_evening_greeting
when topic=smalltalk time=dusk|night
a[guard] : Quiet so far tonight. Let's keep it that way.
a[child] : I'm not tired. I'm not! | Are there really wolves that walk at night? Bad ones?
a : Long day, {b}? | Evening, {b}. Done for the day? | That's the sun gone, then.
b[innkeeper] : Done? My day's just starting.
b[guard] : Not until the bell. Then I'll sleep like the dead.
b[old] : Every day's long at my age. | I've seen more evenings than I can count, and I'm still glad of each.
b[child] : Can I stay up a bit longer? Just a bit?
b : Long enough. | Nearly done. My paws ache. | Done, and glad of it.
a?[friends] : Sit a while with me, then.

scene st_how_are_you
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|friends|family
a[old] : How are you keeping, {b}? | Still on your feet, {b}?
a : How are you, {b}? | Keeping well, {b}? | You look tired, {b}.
b[old] : Older than yesterday. Not as old as tomorrow. | The knees complain, but they still carry me.
b[child] : I found a beetle this big! | I'm bored. There's nothing to do.
b[merchant] : Busy, which is the same as well, for a trader.
b : Well enough. | Can't complain. Well, I can, but I won't. | Tired. But well.
a : Good. That's good. | Glad to hear it. | Look after yourself.

scene st_strangers_nod
when topic=smalltalk band=strangers
a[child] : Who are you? I haven't seen you before. | Are you new? You smell new.
a[old] : I don't think we've met. I'm {a}. | You're not from my street, are you?
a : Good day. | I don't think we've been introduced. {a}. | Fine day, isn't it?
b[child] : I'm {b}. I live just there.
b[guard] : {b}, of the watch. Keep out of trouble and we'll get along.
b[merchant] : {b}. I keep a stall, if you ever need anything.
b : {b}. Good to meet you. | Good day. {b}, if you're asking. | Fine enough, yes.
a?[old] : Hm. Good name. My aunt had a cousin called {b}.

scene st_the_hour
when topic=smalltalk
a : What hour is it, would you say? | Is it past midday already? | Has the bell gone yet?
b[time=dawn] : Barely dawn. The day's not even awake. | Early yet. Too early.
b[time=day] : Past the middle of the day, I'd say. | Hard to tell under this sky. Day, anyway.
b[time=dusk] : Getting on for evening. Look at the light. | Late enough to stop working.
b[time=night] : Night, {a}. Proper night. Shouldn't you be abed? | Late. Too late to be asking.
b : No idea. | I lost track hours ago.
a : Hm. Thank you. | Of course it is. | I'll be late, then.

scene st_feet_ache
when topic=smalltalk
a[old] : My feet ache from here to my ears. | These old paws weren't made for cobbles.
a[laborer] : I've carried half the town on my back today. | Every bone I own is complaining.
a[farmer] : Furrow after furrow since dawn. My back's like a bent nail.
a : My feet are killing me. | What a day. I'm worn to the bone. | I need to sit down before I fall down.
b[healer] : Soak them in warm water with salt. And stop walking so much.
b[child] : I could run all day and all night!
b[old] : Wait till you're my age.
b : Sit, then. The step's free. | You and everyone else. | Tell me about it.
a : If I sit I'll never get up again. | Maybe I will.

scene st_food_talk
when topic=smalltalk
a[child] : I'm hungry. When's supper? | I'd eat a whole loaf if you let me.
a[baker] : There'll be a fresh batch out by noon, if you're passing.
a[cook] : I've a stew on that wants another hour. Smells right, though.
a : I could eat a horse. | What I'd give for something hot. | Have you eaten today?
b[child] : Me too! Me too!
b[innkeeper] : There's soup at mine, and bread, for a fair price.
b[old] : Eat while you've the teeth for it.
b : Me too. | Not since morning. | Not enough, anyway.
a?[friends] : Come and eat with us tonight, then. There's always enough for one more.

scene st_sleep_talk
when topic=smalltalk time=day|dusk
a : I barely slept last night. | Did you hear the noise last night? | I slept like a stone.
b[old] : I never sleep past the third hour any more. | The young sleep. The old lie awake and think.
b[child] : I had a dream about a fish as big as a house!
b[guard] : I was the noise last night. Someone had to shout at the drunks.
b : Nor me. | Something kept me awake, too. | Lucky you.
a : Tonight, then. Tonight I'll sleep. | Ah, well.

scene st_old_days
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=old
a : Things aren't what they were, {b}. | When I was young, this street was all grass. | I remember when bread cost half a penny.
b[old] : They never were, {a}. That's the joke of it. | You remember wrong, old friend. It was worse.
b[child] : Was there really grass here? Where did it go?
b[young] : So you keep saying.
b : I'm sure. | Was it better, then? | If you say so, {a}.
a : Better? No. Slower. | Ha. You'll see, one day. | Different. Just different.

scene st_children_play
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=young|adolescent b.stage=young|adolescent
a : Do you want to play? | Race you to the corner! | I found a stick that looks like a sword.
b : Yes! | Only if I'm the guard this time. | You'll lose. You always lose.
a : I will not! | Fine, you can be the guard. | Go!

scene st_children_secret
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=young|adolescent
a : Can you keep a secret? | I know something nobody else knows. | Promise you won't tell?
b[child] : Cross my heart. | Tell me tell me tell me!
b[old] : I've kept a few in my time. Go on, then.
b[guard] : That depends on the secret, little one.
b : I promise. | What is it? | Go on.
a : There's a nest under the bridge. With eggs. | I saw a ghost. A real one. | I'm not telling after all.

scene st_young_bored
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=adolescent
a : There's nothing to do in this place. | I'm going to leave one day. See the world. | Everyone here is so old.
b[old] : The world will still be there when you're grown. | I said the same thing at your age.
b[adolescent] : Me too. We could go together. | Where would you even go?
b : You'll miss it when you're gone. | Mind your manners. | And who'd do your chores?
a : I won't. | I'd go anywhere. | Somewhere with more than one street.

scene st_courting
when topic=smalltalk band=friends|acquaintances a.stage=adult b.stage=adult
weight 0.6
a : You've done something with your fur. It suits you. | You look well today, {b}. | Would you walk with me later?
b : Oh! Thank you. | Have I? I hadn't noticed. | Maybe. If you're lucky.
a : I'll take that as a yes. | I noticed. | I'll be by the well at dusk.
b?[friends] : Then I'll be there.

scene st_spouse_morning
when topic=smalltalk band=spouses
a : Did you bank the fire before you left? | You were snoring again. | Don't forget the bread on your way home.
b : I did. I think. | I never snore. | I won't. I'll forget, but I won't.
a : You did not. | Like a saw through wet wood. | You always say that.
b?[time=dusk] : Come home. I'm tired of this day.

scene st_family_supper
when topic=smalltalk band=family
a : Mother wants us all home for supper tonight. | Have you seen the little ones? | Who left the door open?
b[child] : I didn't! It wasn't me!
b[old] : I'll be there, if my legs get me there.
b : I'll be there. | Somewhere about. | Not me.
a : Don't be late. | They'll turn up hungry. | Well, somebody did.

scene st_neighbour_noise
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|rivals place=home|street
a : Your pups were howling half the night. | Was that you singing, last night? | Your shutter bangs every time the wind changes.
b[rivals] : And your hearth smokes into my window. We're even. | Mind your own house.
b : Sorry. I'll speak to them. | It was not! Well. Maybe. | I'll fix it. One day.
a : See that you do. | It's fine. Just mention it. | One day. Right.

scene st_lent_tool
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|friends|family
a : Do you still have my good knife? | Can I borrow your ladder tomorrow? | You never brought back my basket.
b : It's around somewhere. | Of course. I'll bring it by. | Didn't I? I'm sure I did.
a : Somewhere isn't here, {b}. | Thank you. | You didn't.
b?[friends] : I'll find it tonight, I swear.

scene st_money_short
when topic=smalltalk band=friends|family
a : Things are tight this month. | I've not a penny to my name till next week. | Could you spare a little, until the end of the week?
b[merchant] : Trade's slow for me too. But here, take this.
b[old] : When was it ever not tight?
b : I've little enough myself. | I'll see what I can do. | Times are hard for everyone.
a : I know. Forget I asked. | You're good to me. | We'll manage.

scene st_good_mood
when topic=smalltalk
a : You're cheerful today. | Something's put a spring in your step. | Why are you grinning like that?
b[child] : I'm always cheerful! | I got a sweet!
b[old] : I woke up. At my age, that's reason enough.
b[spouses] : You, of course.
b : Am I? Must be the weather. | Good news, that's all. | Can't a body smile?
a : Well, keep it up. | Tell me later. | Suit yourself.

scene st_bad_mood
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|friends|family
a : What's eating you? | You look like thunder. | Who stepped on your tail?
b : Nothing. Leave it. | Everything. And nothing. | Don't ask.
a : As you like. | I'm here if you want to talk. | I won't, then.
b?[friends] : Later. Maybe later.

scene st_lost_thing
when topic=smalltalk
a : Have you seen a little leather pouch? | I've lost my good comb. | I put my knife down and now it's gone.
b[child] : I didn't take it! | Is there a reward?
b[guard] : Report it at the watch house, if it doesn't turn up.
b : Not today. | Where did you see it last? | Sorry, no.
a : If I knew that it wouldn't be lost. | Never mind. | It'll turn up.

scene st_rumour_mill_small
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|friends
a : Anything happening I should know about? | Heard anything good lately? | What's the talk today?
b[merchant] : Only that prices go up and nobody's happy.
b[guard] : Nothing I'm allowed to say.
b[innkeeper] : I hear everything, and I repeat nothing. Mostly.
b[old] : Same as every day. Somebody's sick, somebody's married, somebody's dead.
b : Nothing much. | Quiet, for once. | Not a word.
a : Pity. | That's a mercy. | Well, keep your ears open.

scene st_weather_ahead
when topic=smalltalk weather=clear|overcast
a : Think it'll hold? | Fine day for it. | Clouds over the hills. Might turn.
b[farmer] : It'll hold till dusk. After that, I'd not swear to it.
b[fisher] : The water says otherwise. There's a turn coming.
b[old] : My knee says rain by morning. My knee is never wrong.
b : I hope so. | Might do. | We'll see.
a : Let's hope. | Your knee's been wrong before. | Always "we'll see".

scene st_work_waiting
when topic=smalltalk
a[merchant] : Quiet day. Nobody buying. | I've sold three things since dawn. Three.
a : Back to work, I suppose. | No rest for the likes of us. | Well, this won't get the work done.
b[child] : I don't have to work! I'm little!
b[old] : I did my working years. Now I watch.
b : No rest at all. | It never ends. | Go on, then.
a : Lucky you. | Wish me luck. | Off I go.

scene st_age_compare
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=adult b.stage=old
a : How long have you lived here now, {b}? | You must have seen this place change.
b : Longer than you've been alive, pup. | Too long, and not long enough. | I saw them lay these very stones.
a : I believe it. | Tell me about it some time. | Hard to imagine.
b?[friends] : Some evening. Bring something to drink.

scene st_young_and_old
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=old b.stage=young|adolescent
a : Mind your manners, young one. | You'll be taller than me by spring. | Do you help your mother at home?
b : Yes, {a}. | I'm already taller than my sister! | Sometimes. When she makes me.
a : Good. Good. | Ha. You'll be taller than all of us. | Sometimes is better than never.

scene st_tavern_round
when topic=smalltalk place=tavern
a[innkeeper] : Another? You've the look of someone with one more in them.
a : Another round? | This ale's thinner than it used to be. | Busy tonight.
b[innkeeper] : Thin? I'll have you know it's exactly as thin as last year.
b[guard] : Just the one. I'm on at dawn.
b[old] : Thinner than my hair. Pour it anyway.
b : Go on, then. | Everything's thinner than it used to be. | Too busy. Can't hear myself think.
a : That's the spirit. | Ha. True enough. | Then stop thinking and drink.

scene st_tavern_song
when topic=smalltalk place=tavern time=dusk|night
a : Someone start a song. | Not that song again. | Who taught that pup to sing? Someone should untaught him.
b[old] : When I was young we knew songs worth singing.
b[innkeeper] : Sing all you like, so long as you buy as you sing.
b : You start it. | It's the only one they know. | His mother, and she should be ashamed.
a : Not likely. | Then teach them another. | Ha.

scene st_market_bustle
when topic=smalltalk place=market
a : What a crush today. | Everyone and their pups are out. | I can't get to the stalls for the crowd.
b[merchant] : A crowd is a good day, for those of us selling.
b[guard] : Watch your purse in a crush like this.
b : Market days are always like this. | Go early, that's the trick. | Follow me. I know a way round.
a : Is it? I hadn't noticed. | Too late for that. | Lead on.

scene st_chapel_quiet
when topic=smalltalk place=chapel
a : Peaceful in here. | I come here to think, mostly. | Did you light a candle?
b[priest] : The peace is what it's for. Stay as long as you need.
b[old] : I come to remember the ones who are gone.
b : It is. | Me too. | Two. One for each of my parents.
a : That's a good thing. | They'd be glad of it. | Mm.

scene st_home_visit
when topic=smalltalk place=home band=friends|family|spouses
a : Sit, sit. You're letting the heat out. | Mind the step; it's loose. | Shall I put something on the fire?
b : Thank you. | I always forget that step. | Only if you're having some.
a : Of course I am. | Everyone does. | There. Warm yourself.

scene st_gate_talk
when topic=smalltalk place=gate
a[guard] : Name and business, and be quick about it.
a : Busy on the road today. | Look at the dust on that wagon. | Anyone interesting come through?
b[guard] : Only the usual. Carters, peddlers, the odd fool.
b[carter] : Busy for me, aye. Three loads before noon.
b : A few. Nobody worth mentioning. | Dust everywhere. | Not that I saw.
a : Glad to hear it. | Rather you than me. | Well, keep an eye out.

scene st_field_break
when topic=smalltalk place=field
a[farmer] : Rest a moment. The field's not going anywhere. | Look at that sky. Good growing weather.
a : Hard ground this year. | Is that the last row? | I'll be finding stones in my dreams.
b[farmer] : It's always hard ground. That's farming. | Last row, then home.
b[child] : Can I help? I'm strong!
b : It is. | Nearly. | Me too.
a : Back to it, then. | Thank the stars. | Ha.

scene st_shore_talk
when topic=smalltalk place=shore
a[fisher] : Water's got a mood on it today. | Fish are deep. They know something.
a : Smell that air. | Look at the water. | Cold wind off the water.
b[fisher] : It always smells like that. You get used to it. | They always know something.
b[child] : Can I go in? Can I?
b : Salt and rot. Lovely. | It's never the same twice. | Always is.
a : I never do. | True enough. | Mind the edge.

scene st_wild_road
when topic=smalltalk place=wild
a : Long way from anywhere out here. | Keep an eye on the trees. | I don't like this stretch of road.
b[guard] : Nor do I. Stay close.
b[carter] : I've driven it a hundred times. It's the hundred-and-first you worry about.
b : We'll be through it soon. | It's quiet. Too quiet. | Nor me.
a : Let's hope so. | Don't say that. | Walk faster, then.

scene st_compliment_work
when topic=smalltalk
a : That's fine work you do. | I hear good things about you. | You've a steady paw, I'll give you that.
b[apprentice] : My master says I'm hopeless.
b[old] : Years of practice. Most of them wasted.
b[child] : I'm good at lots of things!
b : Thank you. | Do you? From whom? | It pays the rent.
a : Then your master's wrong. | Everyone. | It's more than that.

scene st_missing_someone
when topic=smalltalk band=friends|family
a : I keep thinking about my brother. | I miss the way things were. | Do you ever think of leaving?
b[old] : Everyone you miss is still with you, in a way.
b : Have you heard from him? | So do I. | Every day. And then I don't.
a : Not in months. | Well. | Me too.

scene st_dream
when topic=smalltalk
weight 0.7
a : I had the strangest dream. | I dreamt of the sea last night, and I've never seen it. | Do dreams mean anything, do you think?
b[priest] : Some do. Most are only the stomach talking.
b[old] : I've stopped dreaming. Or stopped remembering.
b[child] : I dreamt I could fly!
b : Tell me. | Did you? | Only that you ate too late.
a : I've forgotten already. | Strange, isn't it? | Ha. Probably.

scene st_fur_shedding
when topic=smalltalk season=spring|summer
a : I'm shedding like a pine in a storm. | There's fur on everything I own. | Spring coat's coming in at last.
b[old] : At my age it doesn't grow back. Count your blessings.
b : Me too. Look at my rug. | Brush it outside, at least. | Mine's patchy.
a : Ha. | I'll try. | Nobody's looking.

scene st_winter_coat
when topic=smalltalk season=autumn|winter
a : My winter coat's coming in thick this year. | Feel this cold. | The nights are drawing in.
b[old] : Thick coat, hard winter. That's what they always said.
b[child] : Will it snow? I want it to snow!
b : Mine too. | I feel it in my bones. | Already.
a : Let's hope they're wrong. | Wrap up. | Too soon.

scene st_crow_omen
when topic=smalltalk
weight 0.5
a : Did you see the crows this morning? A whole flock of them. | A black cat crossed my path twice. | I spilled salt at breakfast.
b[old] : Throw some over your shoulder. Quick, before it settles.
b[priest] : Omens are for the idle. Work is for the rest of us.
b : Probably nothing. | I'd stay indoors, if I were you. | Bad luck, that.
a : Probably. | Maybe I will. | Don't say that.

scene st_new_shoes
when topic=smalltalk
weight 0.5
a : Do you like my new collar? | Got a new cloak at last. | My sister mended my old coat; looks new, doesn't it?
b[merchant] : Where did you buy that? Not from me, I'd remember.
b[child] : It's shiny!
b : Very fine. | It suits you. | It does!
a : Ha. Thank you. | I thought so too. | She's clever with a needle.

scene st_story_request
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=young b.stage=old
a : Tell me a story, {b}! | Is it true you once saw a bear? | What was it like when you were little?
b : Once upon a time there was a pup who asked too many questions. | A bear? Three of them. Or one bear, three times. | Colder. Hungrier. We were happy anyway.
a : And then what? | Really? | That doesn't make sense.
b : Then she grew up and asked even more. | Truly. | One day it will.

scene st_farewell
when topic=smalltalk
a : Well, I'll let you get on. | I should be going. | Mind how you go, {b}.
b[child] : Bye! Bye bye!
b[old] : Go well. And come back.
b[guard] : Stay out of trouble.
b : And you. | Go well. | Until next time.

scene st_weekday_plan
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances|friends|family
a : What are you doing with yourself this {weekday}? | Any plans? | Busy week ahead?
b[merchant] : Selling, and hoping to sell more.
b[child] : Playing!
b[guard] : Walking the same streets I always walk.
b : Same as always. | Work, then sleep, then work. | Nothing I'd call a plan.
a : Same as me, then. | Sounds about right. | Ha.

scene st_season_turning
when topic=smalltalk
a : Feels like {season}, now. | The season's turning. | Is it {season} already?
b[old] : Every year they come faster.
b[farmer] : About time. The ground's been waiting.
b : It does. | Already? | Hard to believe.
a : They do. | Isn't it. | Time flies.

scene st_town_pride
when topic=smalltalk
a : Say what you like, there's no place like {town}. | I'd not live anywhere but {town}. | {town} isn't much, but it's ours.
b[adolescent] : I'd live anywhere else, given half a chance.
b[old] : Born here, and I'll be buried here.
b[merchant] : Good place to trade. That's all I ask of a place.
b : Too right. | I've seen worse. | It'll do.
a : You'll come back. Everyone does. | Ha. | It will.
